# matmul — 54x55 hand grid, NOT YET SUBMITTED

grid         54x55   area2 3,025
local        7/7 public cases, avg 13,848.57 ticks, local score 41,891,929
source       tasks/solutions/matmul_hand54.man
problem id   58f54636-3ec4-497d-8102-b486f13a1ed1

Against the live submission (197,437,831 at 76x76 / 34,182 ticks) this is 4.7x
better on both terms at once: 1.91x on area2 and 2.47x on ticks.

Projected judge score depends on the ratio, which is NOT inherited from the old
machine -- submit_guarded's 1.236-1.506 range belongs to the tape-width-bound
build this replaces, and the ratio is a property of the machine. Pass the high
end (2.2) and re-pin from the first judge response:

    ratio 1.0 -> 41.9M (rank 23)   1.35 -> 56.6M (rank 25)
    ratio 1.5 -> 63.1M (rank 28)   2.2  -> 92.2M (rank 31)

Even at 2.2 that is rank 31 against the current rank 38, so the guard passes.

Both optimisers were run against it and found nothing:
  optimize --semantic       one candidate (steer.coalesce_resteer), rejected by verify
  manopt --moves all --infer-capacity --speed-for-space   no improving move

manfree says why: 0/55 rows and 0/54 cols are removable, and 14 of the 16 pipes
are ONE ring group pinned at 801 cells with 0 spare, so no cut is available
without risking a deadlock. The six pipe-only rows each carry 2-4 pipes -- those
are crossing bands, not slack, so a re-route has nothing to avoid. Ceiling if
every one folded is 49 rows / factor 2,916, i.e. 3.6%, and it is not reachable.
This grid is ring-capacity-bound, not geometry-bound.
